<title>GREECE: GREEK BANANA IMPORTER'S CHILLING ORDEAL.</title>
<headline>GREEK BANANA IMPORTER'S CHILLING ORDEAL.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>After refusing to yield to demands for money, two robbers locked Greek banana importer Ioannis Koutroubis in a freezer and he almost froze to death.</p>
<p>Koutroubis, 63, was found by his wife and was on the verge of death, the state ANA news agency reported. He was locked in the freeze after refusing to give money to the robbers, who wore carnival masks.</p>
<p>He was working in his warehouse office in the western port of Patras.</p>
<p>--Dimitris Kontogiannis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
